sections.body:
In CSS, names starting with `--` are **variables**. You define them once and use them everywhere with `var(...)`:

```
:root { --accent: #f7df1e; }
h2 { border-bottom: 4px solid var(--accent); }
button.active { outline: 3px solid var(--accent); }
```

You change them with one line of JavaScript, and **everything** that uses the variable updates at once:

```js
const root = document.documentElement; // :root, that is <html>
root.style.setProperty("--accent", "#b388ff");
const now = getComputedStyle(root).getPropertyValue("--accent").trim();
```

examples.code:
const btn = document.querySelector("#toggle");
btn.addEventListener("click", () => {
  document.body.classList.toggle("night");
  const night = document.body.classList.contains("night");
  btn.textContent = night ? "Day mode" : "Night mode";
});

const slider = document.querySelector("#size");
slider.addEventListener("input", () => {
  const value = slider.value + "px";
  document.documentElement.style.setProperty("--size", value);
  document.querySelector("#label").textContent = value;
});

